            <ArticleTitle>Effectiveness of the electronic medical record in cholesterol management in patients with coronary artery disease (Virtual Lipid Clinic).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>163-5, A5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study demonstrates that the Virtual Lipid Clinic, an electronic medical record with computer-assisted cholesterol management, is associated with improved lipid management in patients with coronary artery disease. In comparison to traditional documentation methods with &quot;pen and paper&quot; charts, outpatient visits utilizing the electronic medical record were associated with a twofold increase in low-density lipoprotein (LDL) documentation, a threefold increase in achieving LDL goal, and a 30% increase in the use of lipid-lowering drugs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
